  "$comment": [
    "DRAFT / NOT EFFECTIVE — SECB-DRAFT-MCP-GATE-SEED-001, 2026-07-31.",
    "",
    "A candidate registry seed giving each agent that would front through SecB its",
    "OWN identity, drafted at operator request for review. It is NOT wired into any",
    "launcher and NOTHING reads it: tools/start-secb-mcp.mjs still defaults to",
    "tests/fixtures/valid/mcp-registry-seed.example.json. Adopting this file means",
    "pointing SECB_MCP_REGISTRY_SEED at it, which is an operator act.",
    "",
    "Why one identity per agent rather than one shared identity: every per-caller",
    "control in the server keys on agent_instance_id. Sharing one id across agents",
    "makes the rate limit a single pool that any one agent can exhaust for all,",
    "makes the classification ceiling the same for every agent regardless of what",
    "each is trusted with, and makes the invocation ledger unable to say WHICH",
    "agent made a call. Those controls do not fail loudly when the id is shared —",
    "they just quietly stop distinguishing anything.",
    "",
    "Ceilings below are deliberately conservative and are the operator's to change.",
    "authority_ceiling A0 is the lowest and matches the existing example seed;",
    "max_data_classification is set per agent by what that agent is actually used",
    "for, not uniformly, because a uniform value is the same mistake as a shared id."
  ],
